$ grep_lite ferry < data/harbour.txt
A ferry left for the island at six.
No ferry runs on Sunday.
[exit 0]
$ grep_lite -i -n ferry < data/harbour.txt
2:A ferry left for the island at six.
3:No ferry runs on Sunday.
5:FERRY TIMES ARE POSTED AT THE PIER.
[exit 0]
$ grep_lite -v -n island < data/harbour.txt
1:The harbour lights came on at dusk.
3:No ferry runs on Sunday.
5:FERRY TIMES ARE POSTED AT THE PIER.
6:Gulls followed the boats home.
[exit 0]
$ grep_lite -c -i the < data/harbour.txt
5
[exit 0]
$ grep_lite lighthouse < data/harbour.txt
[exit 1]
